ARG BASE_IMAGE=grafana/mcp-grafana:2.3.0-alpine
# Rebuild the pinned v2.3.0 source with a patched Go toolchain. Keep the
# upstream runtime image so its user, entrypoint, and transport defaults remain.
# Update the source revision and version together with repackaging/images.yaml.
FROM golang:1.27.4-alpine AS builder
ENV GOTOOLCHAIN=local
RUN apk add --no-cache git
WORKDIR /src
RUN git init && git remote add origin https://github.com/grafana/mcp-grafana.git && \
    git fetch --depth=1 origin c8cafb67854c45e79f8f9b5fca7d9b3a403f1771 && \
    git checkout --detach FETCH_HEAD
# x/crypto v0.59.0 removes the unmaintained OpenPGP package. Grafana uses
# bcrypt, not OpenPGP, so no application OpenPGP API migration is needed.
RUN go get golang.org/x/crypto@v0.59.0
RUN CGO_ENABLED=0 go build -p 4 -trimpath \
    -ldflags="-s -w -X github.com/grafana/mcp-grafana/v2.version=v2.3.0" \
    -o /out/mcp-grafana ./cmd/mcp-grafana

FROM ${BASE_IMAGE}

USER root
RUN apk upgrade --no-cache
COPY --from=builder --chown=1000:1000 /out/mcp-grafana /app/mcp-grafana
USER mcp-grafana

# Preserve the previous release's telemetry behavior.
ENV GRAFANA_USAGE_STATS=disabled
